$ABCD$ is a cyclic quadrilateral, and $AC$ is a diameter.
$\angle BAC = 28^{\circ}$.
Find $\angle BCA$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (1.732,1);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.798,0.877);
\coordinate (C) at (-1.732,-1);
\coordinate (D) at (0.209,-1.989);
\draw (A) -- (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\pic[draw, "$28^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = B--A--C};
\pic[draw, "$33^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.4cm, angle eccentricity=2] {angle = C--A--D};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$AC$ is a diameter of a circle with centre $O$ and radius $10$ cm.
$BD$ is a chord perpendicular to $AC$ at $M$, with $AM = 2$ cm.
Find $BD$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{calc, angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2,0);
\coordinate (B) at (-1.6,1.2);
\coordinate (D) at (-1.6,-1.2);
\coordinate (M) at (-1.6,0);
\draw (A) -- (C);
\draw (O) circle (2);
\draw (B) -- (M);
\draw (M) -- (D);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[below right] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] at ($(A)!0.5!(M)$) {$2\text{ cm}$};
\coordinate (Ma) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (Mb) at ($(M)!0.3cm!(B)$);
\draw (Ma) -- ($(Ma)+(Mb)-(M)$) -- (Mb);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
